description:
What: Rename the KITH_BASE_URL environment variable to KITHD_BASE_URL in kithd/src/lib.rs, with a deprecated fallback that logs a warning.

Why: All other kithd env vars use the KITHD_ prefix (KITHD_BIND_ADDR, KITHD_DATA_DIR, etc.). KITH_BASE_URL uses the old KITH_ prefix, creating an inconsistency that confuses operators.

Algorithm:
1. In kithd/src/lib.rs (around line 59), find:
     let base_url = std::env::var("KITH_BASE_URL").unwrap_or_else(|_| DEFAULT_BASE_URL.to_string());
2. Replace with:
     let base_url = if let Ok(v) = std::env::var("KITHD_BASE_URL") {
         v
     } else if let Ok(v) = std::env::var("KITH_BASE_URL") {
         eprintln!("kithd: KITH_BASE_URL is deprecated, use KITHD_BASE_URL");
         v
     } else {
         DEFAULT_BASE_URL.to_string()
     };
3. Update the doc comment at lines 32-37 to say KITHD_BASE_URL (not KITH_BASE_URL).
4. Search for any tests in kithd/tests/ or kithd/src/ that set KITH_BASE_URL and update them to KITHD_BASE_URL.
5. Run cargo fmt, cargo clippy, cargo test -p kithd.

Defensive rules:
- Keep the deprecated KITH_BASE_URL fallback so existing deployments don't break silently.
- Only emit the deprecation warning; do not fail.
- Do not change the DEFAULT_BASE_URL constant.

Closes: KITH-v7t.8
